.TH PASSGEN 1
.SH NAME
passgen \- throwaway test password generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B passgen
[\fB\-l\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-c\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-a\fR|\fB\-L\fR|\fB\-d\fR|\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-f\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints random passwords to stdout using /dev/urandom. Meant for test data, not for real accounts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-length " " \fIN\fR
Password length (default 32).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-count " " \fIN\fR
Number of passwords to print (default 1).
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-alnum
Letters and digits.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-letters
Letters only.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-digits
Digits only.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-hex
Hex characters only.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-symbols
Lowercase, digits and symbols (default).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-full
Upper, lower, digits and symbols.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
